#let abstract = [
  TermWise is a web app that helps Oregon State University students build valid term-by-term plans without repeatedly checking the catalog, scheduler, and prerequisite pages. Students select a major (starting with Computer Science), enter completed/planned courses, and drag classes into Fall/Winter/Spring/Summer terms. As the plan is built, TermWise validates prerequisites and term offerings, flags invalid sequences, and summarizes credit load and progress. The system uses a modular client–server architecture with a REST API, a validation engine, and a relational database populated by a small ETL pipeline. Our MVP focuses on a curated course subset, reliable prerequisite validation, and a simple planner UI, with persistence and a basic GPA calculator as supporting features.
]
